{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791149986,"nonce":"yGYv/YRMSPcOE+GxCpweK6myeY4=","title":"tbc 0.3's BC4 encoder picks poor indices, degrading occlusion and normal maps","message":"blinc_game_kit encodes glTF occlusion as BC4 and normal maps as BC5,\nwhich is two BC4 channels, through tbc::encode_image_bc4_r8_conv_u8. The\nencoder's endpoints are right but its per-pixel index often is not the\nnearest palette entry, so both texture kinds are far worse than the\nformat allows.\n\nReported by the ashui session, which measured DamagedHelmet's albedo red\nchannel at 2048x2048: tbc 22.17dB, nearest-of-palette using TBC'S OWN\nENDPOINTS 43.41dB, a plain min/max encoder 43.28dB. tbc's BC1 on the\nsame image is fine, 34.27dB against 34.20dB for a box fit, so this is\nspecific to the BC4 index quantizer.\n\nReproduced independently here on a synthetic gradient, so the finding\ndoes not depend on their data or their decoder:\ncrates/blinc_gpu/tests/bc4_quality.rs encodes a 256x256 channel, decodes\nper the BC4 spec, and compares against the best possible output FOR THE\nENDPOINTS TBC ITSELF CHOSE. tbc 42.56dB, nearest-of-palette 69.05dB, a\ngap of 26.49dB. The test is #[ignore]d so the suite stays green.\n\nUsing tbc's own endpoints is what isolates the fault: the block's two\nendpoints are fine, only the index assignment is wrong.\n\n\n1. Fix it upstream in tbc, or move to a version that has.\n2. Re-pick the indices in Blinc after calling tbc. The endpoints are\n   already in the encoded block, so a pass over the output can replace\n   each 3-bit index with the nearest palette entry. Self-contained,\n   around thirty lines in packages/blinc_game_kit/src/gltf/bc_encode.rs,\n   no dependency change, and worth about +21 to +26dB on AO and normals.\n   Costs one extra pass over the encoded data.\n3. Replace tbc for BC4/BC5 entirely.\n\nOption 2 is the one that needs no decision about dependencies, but it\ndoes mean Blinc carries a correction for a library defect, which is\nworth being deliberate about.","files":null}]}